Check the allocations that upstream's fixes do not cover.

Our own patch (AvP). A crafted setup header can make these allocations fail: an
ordered book's size and a residue's decode table are not limited by the size of
the packet. Upstream's main limits the codebook memory in its unreleased codebook
rewrite (e99e46ed5c), which cannot be taken on its own. Here, a failed allocation
is reported as an error instead of writing through a null pointer. During setup
that refuses the file. Once audio is being decoded, the decoder cannot start:
ov_read returns an error on every call (patch 0018), and the caller has to stop.

